# Attention mechanism facade.
#
# Public import: importa ex "gradus:attention" privata attention
# Depends on: gradus:tensor, gradus:gradient, gradus:nn
#
# S6-G1 (gpu-training-lowering stage-6-delivery.md): first concrete
# static-shape attention primitive — scaled dot-product attention for the
# BERT-tiny fragment shapes (B=2, D=8, H=1), bounded to the S6-G1 caller.
# Shape generics are not available yet; follow the norma:optimizer
# concrete-overload precedent.
#
# Will split into nested leaves when ≥2 attention variants are implemented:
#   gradus:attention/scaled_dot_product  scaled dot-product attention
#   gradus:attention/causal              causal masking
#   gradus:attention/multi_head          multi-head composition
#
# Architectural rule: attention is a building block, not a transformer
# component. This module must not import from gradus:transformer.
# No module owns a backend or device handle.
#
# KNOWN TOOLCHAIN CONSTRAINT: every public function in this module is
# self-contained (tensor ops only, no calls to other Gradus functions) — the
# FMIR stepper cannot resolve calls FROM a library function TO another
# library function. The transformer block inlines the same math for the same
# reason (the S4-A train_step_4x4 precedent).
#
# PML0-U3 ledger disposition (pml0-proof-api-ledger.md, gradus 33df687) —
# executed at PML1-U6: scaled_dot_product_2x8 is ADMITTED as caller-backed
# public API (grep-verified live callers in package code):
#   row 12 — bert-tiny-fragment train.fab:366 (+oracle capture.fab:398);
#            bert-gradus-probe train.fab:364

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# scaled_dot_product_2x8 — single-head attention for B=2, D=8, H=1
#   scores = qb @ kbᵀ · scale,  attn = softmax(scores),  context = attn @ vb
#   qb/kb/vb are the biased Q/K/V projections [2,8]; scale is the [2,2]
#   dk_scale factor (1/sqrt(8) fill, matching the fragment shape).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio scaled_dot_product_2x8(
    tensor<f32, [2,8]> qb,
    tensor<f32, [2,8]> kb,
    tensor<f32, [2,8]> vb,
    tensor<f32, [2,2]> scale
) → tensor<f32, [2,8]> {
    fixum tensor<f32, [8,2]> kt      ← kb.transpone()
    fixum tensor<f32, [2,2]> scores  ← qb.matmul(kt)
    fixum tensor<f32, [2,2]> scaled  ← scores.multiplica(scale)
    fixum tensor<f32, [2,2]> attn    ← scaled.activatio_softmax()
    fixum tensor<f32, [2,8]> context ← attn.matmul(vb)
    redde context
}
